 WARNING: Using DynamoDB involves recurring charge from AWS.
 
-The table created by the backend will provision 5/5 R/W capacity.
-It should be covered by the free tier.
+New tables use on-demand (pay per request) billing by default. AWS charges
+for requests without a provisioned capacity limit. To use provisioned capacity,
+set `billing_mode: provisioned` in the storage configuration. In that mode,
+`read_capacity_units`, `write_capacity_units`, and `auto_scaling` apply.
+The billing mode setting only affects tables created by Teleport; it does not
+change the billing mode of an existing table.
 
